{"availability":"available","full":"inity13/scenariosim-mcp","name":"scenariosim-mcp","description":"Deterministic what-if & scenario simulation MCP server for AI agents — project growth, pricing, churn, costs, hiring, runway & unit economics over time, with sensitivity analysis and break-even solving.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-11T11:07:23Z","updated":"2026-10-07T08:20:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://scenariosim-mcp.pages.dev","topics":["ai-agents","break-even","cloudflare-workers","deterministic","financial-modeling","llm","mcp","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","scenario-simulation","sensitivity-analysis","streamable-http","what-if-analysis"],"demo":"https://scenariosim-mcp.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T17:58:22.913Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T17:58:22.913Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T17:58:22.913Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T14:48:18.881Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T15:37:15.214Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T19:03:37.613Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T17:58:22.913Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A transparent, 100% deterministic Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives LLM agents a reliable what-if / scenario simulation engine.","Agents are good at describing a plan but unreliable at projecting it: they drift on multi-period arithmetic, mishandle compounding, and can't show their work. ScenarioSim offloads the simulation to an exact, explainable engine. You provide assumptions (growth rates, churn, pricing, costs, starting metrics, a time horizon); it returns projected outcomes over time, key metrics, the exact assumptions used, plus sensitivity analysis and break-even solving — each with a plain-language explanation.","Every number flows through decimal.js at 40-digit precision (never floats), so identical inputs always produce byte-identical output. The server is stateless — no database, no sessions, no clocks or randomness in the result."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inity13/scenariosim-mcp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3cc50e8f6e10d3b89cf6c669db22356f2904487912a9f29aaf050c2d8bb9e2b2","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T14:48:19.213Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:37.686Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A transparent, 100% deterministic Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives LLM agents a reliable what-if / scenario simulation engine.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inity13/scenariosim-mcp/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"You provide assumptions (growth rates, churn, pricing, costs, starting metrics, a time horizon); it returns projected outcomes over time, key metrics, the exact assumptions used, plus sensitivity analysis and break-even solving — each with a plain-language explanation.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inity13/scenariosim-mcp/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Self-host for unlimited calls with no keys.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inity13/scenariosim-mcp/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"3cc50e8f6e10d3b89cf6c669db22356f2904487912a9f29aaf050c2d8bb9e2b2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inity13/scenariosim-mcp/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:37.687Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T08:20:19Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/inity13/scenariosim-mcp/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:37.688Z","hash":"3cc50e8f6e10d3b89cf6c669db22356f2904487912a9f29aaf050c2d8bb9e2b2","originalBytes":20780,"storedBytes":20780,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:03:37.613Z","subjects":["Simulation & physics","MCP servers & agents"],"platforms":[],"classification":{"version":4,"method":"local_rules","category":"AI